---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BRAND, sites } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="How We Work: Sources, Checks and Corrections | Tidy Magpie"
  description="The rules every Tidy Magpie site follows: where facts come from, how they are checked, how pre-release information is labelled, and how AI is used."
  path="/how-we-work/"
>
  <section class="page">
    <h1>How we work</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The same rules apply to every {BRAND} site. They are here so you can tell where a fact came from and how far to
      trust it.
    </p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Where facts come from</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Official sources come first: a publisher's or agency's own announcements, store pages and data feeds.</li>
        <li>When a news outlet is the source, it is named next to the fact.</li>
        <li>
          Every site has a Sources page that lists each source, what it was used for and the date it was last checked.
        </li>
        <li>A claim has to be traceable to a page we can link to. If it is not, it does not go in.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Checking</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Before a page is published, the facts on it are compared with the sources they cite. Anything that cannot be
          confirmed is cut, or attributed to whoever reported it.
        </li>
        <li>
          Where a site works something out from data, such as the aurora verdict or a tracker's count, the rules are
          covered by automated tests.
        </li>
        <li>Pages are checked on a phone-sized screen and a desktop-sized one.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we do not know</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Details that have not been announced are listed as unannounced. They are not guessed.</li>
        <li>Pre-release and beta information is labelled, and checked again once the real thing is out.</li>
        <li>Live readings show the time they were taken. When a feed is down, the page says so.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Updates and corrections</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Each site keeps a log of changes on its Sources page.</li>
        <li>
          If you find a mistake, <a href="/contact/">tell us</a>. Corrections are made in the data and noted in that
          log.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Original writing, no borrowed artwork</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Text is written for the site, in our own words. Names of characters, achievements and places are used as
          names.
        </li>
        <li>
          No game artwork, screenshots or trailer stills are used. The icons and illustrations are drawn for the sites.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How AI is used</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The sites are researched, written and coded with AI tools. A person decides what gets made and what gets
          published.
        </li>
        <li>
          AI output is never the source for a fact. Each fact is checked against a page that can be cited, as described
          above.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Independence</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          {BRAND} is not affiliated with, sponsored by or endorsed by the companies and agencies whose games and data
          its sites cover.
        </li>
        <li>There is no sponsored content and there are no affiliate links.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The sites these rules cover</h2>
      <ul>
        {sites.map((s) => (
          <li><a href={s.url}>{s.name}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
